-----------------------------------

The easiest way:

@RequestBody :

HTTP request
     to
Java object

@ResponseBody :

Java object
     to
HTTP response

So they work in opposite directions.

In @RequestBody

Client sends:

{
    "name": "Sneha",
    "department": "IT",
    "salary": 70000
}

Spring converts this JSON to:

JSON
 |
Employee Java object

That's:

@RequestBody Employee employee

In @ResponseBody

Out controller returns Java Object:
Employee employee

Spring converts:

Employee Java object
 |
JSON

That's @ResponseBody.